From: Nothing Tetris port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] sensorhub: reject any mismatched sensor list reply

The Nothing OS 4.1 device-module source at
ee2be53cb75670b548948636a0db1d1ff112bf12 accepts a list reply unless all
three correlation fields differ. Notifications are dispatched by command,
so a stale LIST reply with a different sequence normally passes this test.
Its write position can then be used to read an unrelated sensor inventory.

Require all correlation fields to match before consuming the write position.
Keep the existing error, unlock and bounded retry behavior. This adds no
firmware, power, reset, DT or module activation and is not wired to APKBUILD.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/sensor/2.0/sensorhub/sensor_list.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/sensor/2.0/sensorhub/sensor_list.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/sensor/2.0/sensorhub/sensor_list.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/sensor/2.0/sensorhub/sensor_list.c
@@ -80,8 +80,8 @@ static int sensor_list_seq_get_list(struct sensor_info *list,
 	}
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&rx_notify_lock, flags);
-	if (rx_notify.sequence != notify.sequence &&
-	    rx_notify.sensor_type != notify.sensor_type &&
+	if (rx_notify.sequence != notify.sequence ||
+	    rx_notify.sensor_type != notify.sensor_type ||
 	    rx_notify.command != notify.command) {
 		pr_err("reply fail\n");
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&rx_notify_lock, flags);
